From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 11:59:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(equipment): publish what the work runs on, and a GBP
 ready to claim (#33)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every hardwood company in the GTA sells the same four adjectives. None of
them publishes what the adjectives are made of. "Dust-free" is a claim about
an extraction system; "we match the repair" is a claim about a moisture
meter; "the stair does not move" is a claim about anchorage into structure.

/equipment turns those into ten checkable specifications — belt sander,
edger, multi-disc, dust containment, moisture meter, nailer, trowel, finish
application, stair bench, railing anchorage. Each answers what the machine
does, what it means for the floor you end up with, and how to tell on a quote
whether it is in play. Those questions are framed as ones to ask everyone
quoting you, not only us.

The honesty rule, enforced rather than commented: this layer describes what
the work REQUIRES, never what we own. tests/equipment.test.ts fails on any
"we own/run/use" construction in prose, on any of sixteen brand names, on a
missing disclosure in either page's markup or either agent surface, and on a
Product node where DefinedTerm belongs. Blocker #13 documents the ten
photographs that convert the section into a real inventory, and says the test
changes in the same commit as the photographs.

Wired end to end: service pages gain "What this job runs on", method pages
gain "What this method runs on", alsoCalled feeds the search index so
"buffer" and "drum sander" resolve, and both llms surfaces publish the layer
with the caveat attached.

docs/GBP_LAUNCH.md: the profile is ready to claim. Core municipalities are
exactly 20 — Google's cap, no trimming. NAP is one tested string. Eight
services with published bands. Reviews stay null and the schema stays gated.
Two traps stated: do not upload the AI renderings (Google prohibits stock and
off-location images, and photo violations suspend profiles), and the name is
exactly "Green Hardwood" with no city and no keyword.

362 tests pass (+18). 404 prerendered pages (+11). Audit clean.
6 routes x 4 viewports, no horizontal overflow.

